  "title": "False-pass hunt: a both-states control for every synthesis-level gate",
  "question": "Question: which Phase 14 gate could pass while the thing it guards is broken? Target: for each gate shipped by this bucket, construct the known-BROKEN state, confirm the gate FIRES there, and confirm it is SILENT on the known-good state. A probe silent in both states measures nothing -- measured on this estate when a codex-exec probe printed no parse error in either state and was one step from being reported as verification. Scope is what makes this unit necessary rather than a third copy: TST-0018 scans the detectors that already exist at Phase 0 baseline and BLD-0040 inventories the program at Phase 13, both of which run BEFORE any Phase 14 gate exists. Also distinct from SYN-0027, which asks whether the lenses commit the defects they audit.",
  "answer": "Nine Phase-14 synthesis gates (SYN-0002, SYN-0013, SYN-0016 through SYN-0021, SYN-0030) were each run on a known-broken fixture and a known-good fixture created for this unit. Every row records both exit codes. All nine predicates FIRE on broken (non-zero) and are SILENT on good (zero), so verdict=VALID. A planted inert detector is SILENT-IN-BOTH and fails the matrix. Reverting one defect per gate (mutation sweep) turns that gate red. Producing-unit receipts are absent on this worktree; the predicates run here are the control harness specified by those units, not a claim that SYN-0002..SYN-0030 have shipped. SUCCESS:SYN-0040 emitted only when the artifact at output_path exists, is non-empty, parses against output_schema, and every gate has both exit codes recorded and no gate is VALID without them. Any other terminal state is FAILED:SYN-0040 <classification> with the diagnostic tail attached.",
  "completion_sentinel": "SUCCESS:SYN-0040 emitted only when the artifact at output_path exists, is non-empty, parses against output_schema, and every gate has both exit codes recorded and no gate is VALID without them. Any other terminal state is FAILED:SYN-0040 <classification> with the diagnostic tail attached.",
  "rule_3b": "both-states: fire on known-broken, silent on known-good (cited rules/common/single-signal-verification.md; present_on_disk=True)",
  "scope_note": "TST-0018 inventories Phase-0 detectors and BLD-0040 inventories the Phase-13 program; neither sees these Phase-14 gates. SYN-0027 asks whether review lenses commit the defects they audit. SYN-0040 asks whether the gates fire at all.",
